<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Haiti</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Haiti is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> country that occupies the western part of the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispaniola">Hispaniola</a>, formerly the French colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-domingue">Saint-Domingue</a>. Many of its enslaved population came from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoruba">Yoruba people</a> from the region of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo Empire</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haitian-vodou">Haitian Vodou</a> carries elements of Yoruba religion, an example of the Oyo legacy in the Atlantic world.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/haiti.jpg" alt="Haiti" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: (colours and size changes of the now deleted versions) Madden, Vzb83, Denelson83, Chanheigeorge, Zscout370 and Nightstallion … · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Haiti.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
